  "interpretation": [
    "The online badge excludes bots, whereas arena.activePlayers includes alive bots and humans and excludes dead players/remnants. 51–54 entities and 128–167 parts are simulated for 5–7 human arena connections.",
    "Main-thread sampling identifies room simulation, preparing/dispatching network snapshots, and arena-progress transactions as principal costs. Worker postMessage and record copies remain visible. Pet-shield changes and UI code are not identified as dominant hotspots in this sample; that is not proof of zero overhead.",
    "No sustained CPU quota, memory-pressure, disk-I/O or database backlog bottleneck was observed. The game used about one CPU core in total from its six-core quota during this minute. Spare cores do not eliminate work serialized on the main thread.",
    "RSS is comparable to the previous active-game observation; this short sample cannot prove absence of a memory leak. Disk reserve remains small (~1.26 GB), but observed I/O pressure is low.",
    "The +5% camera change can increase visible objects and packet size, up to about 10.25% area for an uncapped two-dimensional view; actual traffic impact was not measured and must not be presented as the proven cause.",
    "The public test-mode activeBots value describes only the legacy primary bot instance, while humanPlayers is summed across rooms. Do not treat activeBots=0 there as proof that all room bots are disabled."
  ],
  "nextTargets": [
    "Reduce arena-progress draft/table copies with exact WAL, duplicate/retry and clan/achievement equivalence checks; keep reliable acknowledgements after durable storage.",
    "Reduce repeated room snapshot preparation and worker serialization while preserving per-peer event/sequence continuity.",
    "Measure independent room execution with the same captured workload; preserve bot split/W/booster behavior rather than hiding load by disabling bots."
  ],
